course: dictionary
lesson: 9704
title: Sulk and the feelings behind it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sulk is when you go quiet and bad-tempered because you are annoyed, or because you did not get what you wanted. «Ella sulked — "it's not fair, I saw it first" — but at bedtime she said sorry.» The words around sulked tell you what happened: she was cross, and she did not say so in a friendly way.
explain: Sulk can be a verb or a noun. As a verb it changes: sulk, sulks, sulked, sulking. As a noun it means a time of being in a bad mood. «By breakfast the sulk had faded» uses it as a noun. Phrases like «in a sulk» and «go off in a sulk» show the same idea.
explain: Look at what happens next in a story. «Toad sulks for a moment, then admits he is "a bit of a talker".» Toad's sulk is short, and he owns up to what he did. Stories often show a sulking character who needs a friend to cheer them up.
explain: Sulking is a way of showing anger or hurt without using words. «Sulking usually takes away more than the loss did.» Staying cross and quiet can leave you worse off, so it is better to calm down and say what is wrong.
fact: Sulk means to stay silent and bad-tempered because you are annoyed or did not get what you want.
fact: As a noun, a sulk is a time of being like this, as in «in a sulk».
fact: «Sulked» is the past tense of the verb: «Ella sulked».
fact: Sulking can show anger or hurt without any words being said.
fact: It is better to calm down and say what is wrong in words.
exercise: «Ella sulked — "it's not fair, I saw it first" — but at bedtime she said sorry.» What does sulked mean here? | Ran all the way home | Fell fast asleep | *Stayed silent and bad-tempered | Laughed loudly and danced
exercise: «By breakfast the sulk had faded.» In this sentence, what kind of word is sulk? | A kind of breakfast food | *A noun, meaning a time of being in a bad mood | A place where sheep live | A verb, meaning to dance
exercise: According to the lessons, what is the best way to deal with a sulk? | Shout at everyone in the room | *Calm down and say what is wrong in words | Hide the cake so nobody else can have any | Stay quiet for as long as possible
test: Toad sulks for a moment, then admits he is «a bit of a talker». What does admits mean here? | Forgets it completely | Hides from it | *Owns up to it, agreeing it is true | Shouts about it
test: Ella was ___ all morning because she did not get the first turn. | counting | dancing | *sulking | painting
exam: In «Sulking usually takes away more than the loss did», what is the author saying? | *Staying cross can leave you worse off than the thing that upset you | A loss is always bigger than a sulk | Sulking makes you taller | Sulking is always fun
